LANGUAGE English

BOOK Halls ORDERED NO KEEP LOOP

	PAGE ExploreHall1
		TRIGGERED BY @ExploreHall1
		
		PROLOG """
			The door has a dirty push plate. When you push on it, you discover
			it's locked. An investigator with the {c:QItemBrassKey} can open
			this door.
		"""
		BUTTON "Explore"
		
		TEXT """
			When you open the door, the rush of cold, stale air sends a chill
			down your spine.

			You stop for a moment and look back down at the footsteps leading
			to this door. You wonder how the air feels so stale if this door
			has been opened recently.
		"""
	
		$mythosHall = TRUE
		exploredHall1 = TRUE AFTER
	END ExploreHall1

	PAGE PlaceHall1
		TEXT """
			You look through the doorway to find a hall. It is clear that it
			was intended for the servants:  plain and dark. Place the
			{c:TileHall1} tile, a door, and a wall as indicated.
			
			Move one space space into the hall.
		"""
						
		REMOVE TokenExploreHallway1ViaDiningRoom
		
		ADD TileHall1, TokenDoorHall1, TokenWallHall1
	END PlaceHall1
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Gallery
		TEXT """
			To your immediate right is a door. Place an Explore token as
			indicated.
		"""
		
		ADD TokenExploreGalleryViaHall1
	END PlaceHall1Gallery
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Painting
		TEXT """
			On the left, a painting glows with unnatural
			light. You can almost feel it calling to you. You shake it off
			because paintings don't have power. Place a Search token as 
			indicated.
			
			As you look away, you catch something moving in your 
			peripheral vision. You glance back and the painting is still
			lightly glowing, something that suddenly seems more troubling.
		"""
		
		ADD TokenSearchHall1Picture
	END PlaceHall1Painting
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Evidence
		TEXT """
			You look down. The rug on the floor is old and beautiful, if
			dirty and poorly cared for. One corner is folded up and looks
			like it has been that way for years. You should probably put
			it back so you don't trip over it.
			
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		ADD TokenSearchHall1Rug
	END PlaceHall1Evidence
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Sight
		TEXT """
			The hall stretches forward. Place a Sight token as indicated.
			
			As you look around, something doesn't feel right.
			You feel like you are being watched.
		"""
		
		ADD TokenSightHall2ViaHall1
		
		IF foundJournal THEN EXIT
	END PlaceHall1Sight
	
	PAGE PlaceHall1Journal
		TEXT """
			<i>The book on the floor,</i> you remind yourself. You turn 
			around and step back. Move one space into the {c:TileDiningRoom}.
			
			You look over, see the book, and bend down to pick it up. Gain
			the {c:QItemJournal} unique item.
			
			You look at the book you picked up:  small, thin, and
			leather-bound. You flip through the pages: 	it's a journal.
			The first entry was scrawled last Sunday.

			Maybe you should hold onto it to give back to Benjamin when you
			see him later today. And maybe take a quick look yourself.

			Gain the {c:QItemJournal} Unique Item, then remove its
			Search token. An investigator holding the {c:QItemJournal}
			can interact with it in the app.
		"""
		
		REMOVE TokenSearchDiningRoomJournal
		foundJournal = TRUE
		
		EXIT
	END PlaceHall1Journal
	
	
	PAGE SearchRug
		TRIGGERED BY @SearchHall1Rug
	
		PROLOG "The corner of the rug is folder over."
		BUTTON "Search"
		
		TEXT """
			You lean down to straighten the rug. You play with it for a bit,
			but have trouble getting it to stay flat--the fold has been there
			too long. You lift the rug a little more to try to flatten the
			corner. There's a piece of paper under the rug. You pick it up to
			find it has a diagram of a tabletop with arcane symbols. Maybe
			it's part of some ritual? You’ve heard the people in this town have
			some funny beliefs.

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceHall1} Unique Item and
			1 {clue}, then discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		ADD QItemEvidenceHall1
		REMOVE TokenSearchHall1Rug AFTER
		
		EXIT
	END SearchRug
	
	PAGE SearchPainting
		TRIGGERED BY @SearchHall1Painting
		
		PROLOG "The painting glows with unnatural light."
		BUTTON "Search"
		
		TEXT """
			The painting is a girl, maybe 12 or 13 years old. The work is
			stunning and the girl looks so lifelike, it’s as if she could just
			step through the frame. She’s wearing a white dress and looks
			serious.

			When you blink, you think the painting has moved but you know that
			cannot happen. You also notice that there is no dust anywhere on
			the painting or the frame. You feel like there’s something else
			you've missed, but you dismiss it and turn away. Gain 1 {clue},
			then remove this Search token.
		"""
		
		REMOVE TokenSearchHall1Painting AFTER
	END SearchPainting

	PAGE SearchPainting2
		TEXT """
			As you turn around, you notice two shadows on the wall, yours
			and... you quickly look back at the painting. The girl is not
			there. Startled, you turn to run back to the {c:TileDiningRoom} and
			are brought up short when the girl from the painting is standing in
			front of you.

			Place the Green Girl token as indicated. Shocked, you take 1 Horror
			({will} negates).
		"""
		
		ADD TokenSarah
	END SearchPainting3
	
	
	PAGE SearchPaintingSarah
		TRIGGERED BY @TalkToSarah WHEN UNREAD
		
		TEXT """
			She is a pretty girl in the the first blush of youth--maybe 11 or
			12 years old. She has curly hair with ribbons and a bright white 
			dress that stands out in the dingy hallway.
		"""
	END TalktoSarah
	
	PAGE TalktoSarah2
		TRIGGERED BY @TalkToSarah
		
		PROLOG """
			She looks at you expectantly. She looks like she wants to say
			something, but is holding back. She still looks serious, but also
			concerned and maybe a little afraid. You notice that she seems
			to be glowing. And maybe a bit transparent.

			She will only speak with {c:EventChosenInvestigator}.		
		"""
		BUTTON "Talk to her"
		
		TEXT """
			She brightens up. <<It's good to see you again. I thought you
			had forgotten me after that night. I've missed you.>>

			You are surprised at what she says. <i>Who is this girl? Why does
			she think she knows me?</i>

			The girl walks over and turns to face you. She looks up 
			at you expectantly.

			Move the Green Girl token to your investigator card.
			She will follow you to whatever ends you meet in this house.
		"""
		
		REMOVE TokenSarah AFTER
		foundSarah = TRUE AFTER
		EXIT
	END TalkSarah2
	

	
	
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
END Hallway